    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d387">

                <pb facs="0481" n="383" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg383"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Commission/603: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland (Wilson) to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-12-04T21:00:00+01:00">December 4, 1932—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 4—5:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>55. From Davis and Wilson. Please see final paragraph
                    50, November 25, 9 p.m. We have discussed the suggestion with McCoy and think it is well to let
                    you know that he feels rather strongly that there would be an impropriety in his
                    acting on a committee to find a solution after <pb facs="0482" n="384"
                        xml:id="pg384"/> he had been a member of a commission which had rendered
                    judgment on the case.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
